ething the role of the buff support  is to provide increased damage and or  defensive bonuses to the team  particularly useful and in-game  activities like heroic incursions or  legendary missions where the enemies had  harder and take more damage the crowd  support player is there to slow or take  down large groups of enemies ideal for  slowing down the rate of NPC advancement  these builds are best suited and  activities like resistance or pretty  much anywhere that rushes are catching  your team off-guard  the tactician Authority Sepp is the most  all-round support set  I don't really rate the six piece set  very highly but using the four or five  piece set with something like the  inventive backpack or Barrett's chest  will have you gaining a decent amount of  utility with the one to five set piece  bonuses going directly into skill haste  and skill power thus it gives the most  flexibility in regards to skills crowd  control skills could include the be FB  sticky bomb flashbang sticky bomb either  the air burst or cluster CQ mines and  the flame turret buff skills include  smart cover tactical scanner pulse or  booster shot the reason that this is one  of the most popular choices as a support  role set is because of the flexibility  players can easily and quickly chop and  change between skills depending on the  situation and activity being played  the final measure four piece bonus  states win and range of hostile grenades  and waters diffuses them and adds  grenades to your inventory this alone is  a huge help and considering the massive  amount of grenade spam this game has  this build can be put together in a  couple of different ways focusing  heavily on skill power or firearms so  try this out based on your play style  preference myself I still like to be  able to do some weapon damage so  firearms is my go-to but this doesn't  mean you can't get any support utility  out of your skills skills like flashbang  sticky bomb and booster shot first aid  don't r