 range of  support skills you can use a weapon with  cool-headed synergizes really well with  this build focus more on marking  multiple targets than trying to take  them down on your own don't get me wrong  I love seeing the crazy high DPS numbers  coming off targets when you get to six  stacks but with a decent sniper build  you should be able to take down most  enemies in the game with one two three  hit shots fire Crist is all about fire  in particular the fire turret although a  fairly reliable solo builds it's still a  bit slow with the damage of a time to be  considered a DPS build for the team  again the six piece - thus it is pretty  meant so running the four piece with two  technicians or the five piece with an  inventor vague or barracks chests are a  good alternative because of your  reliance on the turret I'd probably  recommend stacking into electronics but  an exotic like the urban MDR can still  have you're doing quite a bit of damage  as well  your primary skill should obviously be  the flame turret but your secondary  skill is a bit more flexible to continue  with the fire damage theme you may  choose to use air burst seeker mines  this is one of those gray area sets  although this is a fantastic solo set  and would primarily come under the tank  role the increased threat alone has this  drawing enemy fire away from your  squishier teammates allowing them to  spend more time focusing on the NPCs and  less time on their own health on top of  this the six piece set bonus offers a  buff to your team after receiving a  certain amount of damage to the shield  physical damage weapons etc will  increase armor by 30%  an exotic damage grenades will give a  30% increase to weapon damage you can  actually prop the second one on your own  by just throwing a couple of grenades at  your feet the ballistic shield is our  given but I found the bill to be pretty  effective at being the team Reviver to  equip the defib skill and keep your  teammates alive for days 